# (#126) THE PER-NAME OBSERVER GATE, module scope.
#
# `ch` is NAMED by two observer reads, so it keeps today's byte-exact
# bookkeeping: a name-keyed env slot, aot_observe_num on every write, a
# named env read on every read. `total` and `i` are named by NO observer
# read anywhere in the program, so they compile to plain C statics -- the
# emitted C carries no aot_observe_num / aot_get_num_named_ic for them.
#
# Before the per-name gate one `report of ch` demoted EVERY scalar in the
# unit: `i` became a hash lookup by name plus a type check four times per
# iteration (measured: the larger half of the AOT's observer overhead,
# F-OURO-39). What this fixture pins is that the SPLIT changes nothing a
# program prints -- values byte-exact, verdicts byte-exact.
ch is 1.0
total is 0.0
i is 0
loop while i < 12:
    ch is ch * 0.5
    total is total + ch
    i is i + 1
print of f"total {total}"
print of f"i {i}"
print of f"ch {ch}"
print of f"ch-report {report of ch}"
print of f"ch-converged {converged of ch}"
print of f"ch-diverging {diverging of ch}"
